From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfast Patches <belfast-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cut back OSM buildings from the driving lanes by overlap area
 and depth

resolveBuildingRoadConflicts only cut an OSM building back when its share of
the footprint on the driving lanes was 3% or more, and kept (and did not list)
anything under that. A large footprint with a small share is still a wall in
the lane: OSM way 1260690275 (678 m2) has 12 to 15 m2 (1.8 to 2.2%) in the
lanes of a residential street.

The cut now also applies when the overlap is at least 1 m2 and 0.15 m deep past
the cut line (the lanes' edge plus the 0.3 m kerb allowance). A footprint with
that overlap that cannot be cut (holes, a bend, a cut that removes too much) is
listed in the export report with its overlap area and depth, whatever its share.
Hairline overlaps and walls flush with the kerb still stay and are not listed.

Three unit tests: large footprint with a small overlap is cut, a hairline
overlap is left alone, a courtyard footprint is kept and listed.

